WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You've had
such an interesting path

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:04.738
in your acting career 'cause
first you were in the Marines.

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then --
Was it after the Marines

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:09.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
you went to L.A. briefly
and then came back to Indiana?

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, no, no,
before the Marine Corps.

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.513
-Okay, gotcha.
So, you came back, Marine Corps.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.048 line:92%
And then, came back from that,

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:19.753
and then, basically, decided t
go and audition for Juilliard.

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So, that --

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I've met people
who've gone there,

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I've met people
who auditioned.

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:27.093 size:84% position:42%
It seems very intense,
especially, in my head,

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always forget
how young people are

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
when they audition
for Juilliard.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What were the pieces
that you brought to audition

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:35.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause is it three things
that you have to do, usually

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:36.636 line:92%
-Yeah. You have to sing --

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:39.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or, well,
you have to do two monologues,

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:43.810
one a contemporary monologue
and a classical monologue,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then,
you have to sing a song.

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:46.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-So, I sang, um --

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.748 size:84% position:42%
Well, I did a monologue
from a monologue book.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hadn't even read the play.
Um...

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.052 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
That I found
at Barnes &amp; Noble, I think

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Which I don't know if

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.122
Barnes &amp; Noble's around, but
that's another plug, I guess

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, seriously, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.059 size:84% position:42%
You're gonna catch hell
from Amazon for that.

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:01.761 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, which is, like,
the opposite of Amazon.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:02.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
But Amazon's way better.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, of course. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.232 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-For the sake of this.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:10.170
And then, I did the openin
monologue from "Richard III.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-And then I sang

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Happy Birthday."
-Okay.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:13.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, that was my song.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.810
-So, that seems, like the most
right-down-the-middle choice

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:17.477 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, right, yeah.

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:18.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a very intense versio
of "Happy Birthday."

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, I guess that would be
a case where you'd be like

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:21.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'd love to do a song
from 'Oklahoma,'

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:24.150
but I only had the one line.
-Right, yeah, yeah, right.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:28.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right.
-You're part of an organizatio

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
called
Arts in the Armed Services

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
Am I saying that right?
-Arts in the Armed Forces.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:32.926 line:92%
-Arts in the Armed Forces.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is
a great organization.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you're doing
something very cool --

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:39.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
a very cool tie-in
with "Star Wars."

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:42.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's basically this Omaze,
a way people can go on

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:45.171
and donate money for a chanc
for this really cool experience.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.005 line:92%
-Yeah, well, it's cool for us.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
if it's gonna be cool for them

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're supposed to donate --
If I understand this.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:53.313
You donate, and then you get
two tickets to the premiere,

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:55.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is cool,
and then, I meet you

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the red carpet,
which is not a place

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I feel the most at home
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I sign a lightsaber
-Okay.

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:04.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which I'm assuming
someone gives us.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think they bring it.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
That would be really rude
if you were like...

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Right, right.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:09.929
-They meet you and they're like,
"And the lightsaber?"

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Yeah, you got one?"
-Like, "You didn't bring one

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't --"
-Right, right, right.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:16.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Seem, like the chances
you'd have a better hookup

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a lightsaber.
-Right, yeah, yeah.

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:19.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, that's what it is.
You enter, and all the money

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:22.942
goes to this nonprofit,
which I run with my wife,

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we bring
contemporary theater

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.980 size:81% position:41%
to a military audience
all around the country

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all around the world
and has branched out into this

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:32.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
thing where we do
a Bridge Award,

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:35.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
give a $10,000 grant
to anyone in the military

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:35.955 line:92%
to write a play about anything

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:41.294
We do a film screening serie
for, you know, student veterans.

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:42.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's turned into kind of
a cultural hub

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.564
for people in the military
-It's a really cool idea.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.833
Because, I think, if you'r
independent in the military,

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.469
there are so many people who
have no theater in their life.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:50.503
-True.
-And probably think that there's

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:53.439 size:81% position:41%
this real wall to them
being able to access,

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's really cool that
you're bringing it to people

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.809 line:92%
and because I think, obviously

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody would
get something out of it.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:02:59.946 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Oh, yeah, anytime --

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.248
It is, you know, kind of
predominantly in New York.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:05.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, anytime a group
says that this group

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:08.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
won't understand a play
because of their real estate

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
basically where they're from..

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...or nationality or race

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:15.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always just --
none of that makes sense to me

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:19.499
So, we bring, you know,
what we consider is the best of,

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:22.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
American contemporary theater.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:24.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we don't need to.
It's not military-themed,

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:26.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
by any means,
but because we're people,

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:29.142 size:81% position:41%
because the military
is comprised of humans

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:32.712
who understand what it is
we're doing immediately,

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
and the connection is made

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's really cool.
That's a great organization,

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
and congratulations
on everything else.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always such a pleasur
to see you, Adam.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back.
-Good seeing you.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.622 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Adam Driver.

